WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.139 --> 00:00:01.110
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.949
- Oh, my gosh.
- Hi.

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:04.782
(audience applauds)

00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:06.238
- Have y'all met before?

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.799
- No, we've never met, but
come on, eighth appearance,

00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:09.632
I see you.

00:00:09.632 --> 00:00:10.465
- Hey, look at that.

00:00:10.465 --> 00:00:11.550
We've, we've actually met before.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.383
- Stop it.

00:00:12.383 --> 00:00:13.286
- Wait.
- Yeah.

00:00:13.286 --> 00:00:14.119
We dated in high school.

00:00:14.119 --> 00:00:14.952
Oh yeah, that's right.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:16.770
- That was my boo, we went
to prom and everything.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.575
- He was not memorable.
(Danielle laughs)

00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:20.730
You were the one that
laughed at him all the time,

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:21.563
he was talking about.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:22.396
- That's me.

00:00:22.396 --> 00:00:23.340
- Listen, but he had a great suit at prom,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.365
let me tell you that.

00:00:24.365 --> 00:00:25.440
- [Kelly] I tell you, yeah.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.210
I bet you were the guy
that she wanted to show up

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.972
looking like Dumb and
Dumber in those suits, like.

00:00:28.972 --> 00:00:29.980
(Danielle chuckles)

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:30.813
Were you?
- I'd dare you.

00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:31.860
- I think you were probably funny then.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.030
- I don't remember.
- Okay.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.000
- What you don't remember,
is that we had a TLC theme,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.320
so we had silk pajamas, it was
from the "Creep" video, so.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:39.800
- Okay, I love that outfit.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.633
- That's what we were doing.
- I still have them.

00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:41.880
- Yeah, crazy, sexy, cool.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.470
Okay, so wait, I hear that you're working

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.899
with Eddie Murphy now, is that right?

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:46.029
- Oh, God, yes.

00:00:46.029 --> 00:00:46.862
- That's incredible.

00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:48.630
- Yes, I, this is my first movie,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.370
it is called "Candy Cane Lane".

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.203
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:51.203 --> 00:00:53.190
- It is, Eddie Murphy is at the helm

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.070
with Tracee Ellis Ross and
Robin Thede and like...

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.210
- Oh, my God, this cast, wow.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.218
- It's incredible.

00:00:58.218 --> 00:01:02.490
We just did our first Zoom
table read over the holidays

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:06.720
and I was shaking, because I'm
such a huge Eddie Murphy fan.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.510
When I was 13, from like 13 to 16,

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.460
I would watch, rewatch all of his SNLs

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.878
and all of his movies and...
- So incredible.

00:01:12.878 --> 00:01:15.840
- Everything, so like, to
be able to even see my name

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.300
with his, is just a huge dream come true.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.903
- [Kelly] Absolutely.
(audience applauds)

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.210
So, what your character in "Ghost",

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.920
is a ghost from the 1920s?

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.120
- Yes, she's a...
- That's a fun costume.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.702
- 1920s prohibition era jazz singer.

00:01:30.702 --> 00:01:31.535
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:31.535 --> 00:01:32.430
- [Danielle] Her name is Alberta Haynes.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.630
Yes, oh my God.
(audience applauds)

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.230
Child, look at my girl, Rebecca.

00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:36.992
(Danielle laughs)
(audience applauds)

00:01:36.992 --> 00:01:38.460
- So, I didn't know you sang as well.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.293
You do everything.

00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:41.070
- Listen, I didn't know
I sang either, Kelly,

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.169
to be honest.
(Danielle laughs)

00:01:42.169 --> 00:01:44.190
- Wait, are you one of
those people that like,

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:45.720
the actors that's like, "Sure I can sing".

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.107
- Special skills, I was like,

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.397
"Alto, that's what it is, right?"

00:01:49.397 --> 00:01:50.551
(Danielle laughs)

00:01:50.551 --> 00:01:52.350
So, they cast me.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.080
I actually sang in my
audition just in the lines

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.760
and they were like, "Oh,
she must be able to sing".

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.650
I was like, "Y'all, I'm
just playing around".

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.990
So, I've actually had
to start singing lessons

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:01.823
during the process.

00:02:01.823 --> 00:02:04.380
I've done dance lessons and
I wanna learn the Charleston.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.224
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.570
- [Danielle] And all the
dances from the time period.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.820
And I just think playing
this role is so iconic,

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:12.510
because as a black artist,
the 1920s were so incredible

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:13.950
for us at that time, culturally.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.607
And like, I just wanna give her,

00:02:15.607 --> 00:02:18.780
her just do and all those
artists that came before me, so.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.613
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:19.613 --> 00:02:20.837
- Playing this role is just a dream.

00:02:20.837 --> 00:02:21.930
(audience applauds)

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.310
- I love like, as an actor, like,

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.160
y'all get to learn all
these like, different skills

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.360
for your role, that's cool.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.600
Then you end up like
learning all these, these,

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.200
these cool things that nobody
really gets a chance to do

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.280
or...
- I know.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.113
- Takes the time to do.

00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:34.077
- It's amazing.
- Yeah.

00:02:34.077 --> 00:02:36.630
- And it's like, the best
role I've ever played so far

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.070
in my career.
- That's cool.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.170
- Also, getting to work with
the ensemble, Rose McIver,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.910
who I know has been on the
show and Utkarsh Ambudkar.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:42.743
They're...
- Yeah.

00:02:42.743 --> 00:02:45.090
- Are, are the best lead
leads in the business

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.820
and we are just so honored to
be working with them weekly.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.230
- I love your cast, we've had them here.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.170
And Rose actually said that
y'all get very competitive,

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:53.940
like it's a competitive cast.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.190
- Y'all, we almost didn't
have a season two, okay?

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.184
- What? What was the game?

00:02:57.184 --> 00:02:59.700
- Okay, it was between Mancala,

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.980
but I'm gonna tell you the
real game was Scrabble.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.813
- I love Scrabble.

00:03:02.813 --> 00:03:05.820
- Scrabble almost took us out.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:09.000
Richie Moriarty, who plays Pete and

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.300
Asher Grodman who plays
Trevor, the guy with no pants.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.460
They're very good at Scrabble
and I thought I was great.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.010
But Richie had spelled sommelier

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.410
and got a triple word score.
- What?

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.420
- And then, used all of his letters

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.070
and still to this day, I think he cheated.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.720
I'm like, how did you spell sommelier

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.830
with all these letters?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.479
And we stopped talking for months.

00:03:28.479 --> 00:03:31.110
(audience and Kelly laugh)
Months, months.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.463
Richie, I know you cheated.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.040
- That's an incredible word.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:35.920
- Yeah, it's, it's serious.
- Yeah.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:36.990
- It's, it's no joke.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.580
So, we actually decided
as a cast, you know,

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.570
we're not gonna do Scrabble no more.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:40.530
We're just gonna let it go.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.510
- This is, this is
literally me and my sister

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:43.950
and my mother, we'll play Scrabble

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.540
and I don't even know why we play, y'all.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.020
My mother, every time
almost flips the board

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.760
and she, she is like, she's
like, "That is not a word".

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.079
It's always she and my
sister going at each other.

00:03:53.079 --> 00:03:55.980
It's the most enjoyable
time with my family for me.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.360
Are y'all competitive? Are you?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.077
- Yeah, I'm dyslexic, I can't spell...

00:03:59.077 --> 00:04:00.468
(beeping)
(audience laughs)

00:04:00.468 --> 00:04:01.301
- Oh, my God.

00:04:01.301 --> 00:04:02.737
- Oh, I, I look at Scrabble, I'm like,

00:04:02.737 --> 00:04:04.988
"Yeah, these seem to be
all spelled correctly".

00:04:04.988 --> 00:04:06.090
(audience laughs)

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.170
They're all in front of me, yeah.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.330
- Oh, my God, it's amazing how games

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:12.000
that shouldn't be subjective
can still cause such drama.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.346
- That's me and Connect Four too.

00:04:13.346 --> 00:04:14.179
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:14.179 --> 00:04:15.488
Connect Four is, is, I'm a liar.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.321
- I can play Connect Four.

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:17.154
- [Danielle] Yeah, we'll do it, I'm ready.

00:04:17.154 --> 00:04:18.530
- I'm good at that.
- I'm ready, I'm ready.

